<ul class="enc-list"><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/bhadradri-kothagudem-district"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/bhadradri-kothagudem-district.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Bhadradri Kothagudem district</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Bhadradri Kothagudem district is a district in the north-east of Telangana, India, created in 2016 from part of the former Khammam district.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/bhagadatta"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/bhagadatta.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Bhagadatta</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Bhagadatta is a legendary king of Pragjyotisha, the ancient name of Kamarupa in Assam, son of the demon king Naraka.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/bhagalpur"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/bhagalpur.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Bhagalpur</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Bhagalpur is a city in Bihar, India, on the southern bank of the Ganges.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/bhagavad-gita"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/bhagavad-gita.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Bhagavad Gita</span><span class="enc-type">Work / monument</span><span class="enc-snip">The Bhagavad Gita is a Hindu scripture of 700 Sanskrit verses forming part of the Mahabharata epic, probably composed in the last centuries BCE.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/bhagavadgomandal"><span class="enc-name">Bhagavadgomandal</span><span class="enc-type">Work / monument</span><span class="enc-snip">The Bhagavadgomandal is a Gujarati encyclopedia and dictionary compiled under